export const EMBEDDED_POLICY_MARKDOWN: Record<string, string> = {"OMAYA-Terms-of-Service-v1.5.md":"# Terms of Service\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.5\n\n---\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"**Terms**\") govern your access to and use of the website, mobile application, and services operated under the name **OMAYA.io** by **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**, a private limited company incorporated under Company Law No. 18 of 26 December 2019 of the Federal Republic of Somalia (Registration No. LAG/UBI: 12029035324), with its registered office at Aaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia (\"**OMAYA**,\" \"**OMAYA EXCHANGE**,\" the \"**Company**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\").\n\n**Please read these Terms carefully before using our Services.** They form a binding legal agreement between you and OMAYA. By creating an account, accessing the OMAYA.io website or mobile application, or using any of our Services, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and by all policies incorporated into them by reference. **If you do not agree, you must not access or use the Services.**\n\n> **Important — please note:**\n> - Trading and holding digital assets and engaging in foreign exchange carry significant risk, including the risk of losing all of the funds involved. You should read our **Risk Disclosure Statement** before using the Services.\n> - OMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice. Nothing in the Services is a recommendation to enter into any transaction.\n> - Where OMAYA acts as a **local agent for third-party foreign exchange brokers**, your trading relationship is with that broker and not with OMAYA. See Section 7.\n> - In **peer-to-peer (P2P) trading**, OMAYA is only a facilitator and is not a party to the trade between users. See Section 8.\n\n---\n\n## 1. About OMAYA and These Terms\n\n1.1. OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE is a financial services provider based in Mogadishu, Somalia. Our Services include: exchange of digital assets for local payment methods and vice versa (\"Exchange\"); crypto-to-crypto conversions (\"Swap\"); transfers between local payment providers and wallets (\"MoneyX\"); peer-to-peer trading (\"P2P\"); foreign exchange and currency exchange; remittance and payment services; and acting as a local agent for third-party foreign exchange brokers, in each case as further described in these Terms.\n\n1.2. These Terms apply to all users of the Services, whether accessing through the OMAYA.io website, the OMAYA.io mobile application, or any other channel we make available.\n\n1.3. The following policies are incorporated into and form part of these Terms. By agreeing to these Terms, you also agree to them. Where a specific policy conflicts with these Terms on a matter it governs, that policy prevails on that matter:\n\n- **Privacy Policy**\n- **Cookie Policy**\n- **AML/KYC Policy** (public summary)\n- **Risk Disclosure Statement**\n- **Payment Policy**\n- **Referral Program Terms** (where you participate)\n- **Law Enforcement Request Guidelines**\n\n1.4. We may publish additional product-specific terms, limits, or guidelines for particular features. Where we do, they apply in addition to these Terms.\n\n1.5. **Regulatory status and scope.** OMAYA holds a Commercial Licence issued by the Ministry of Commerce, a licence from the Central Bank of Somalia, and a licence from the Banadir Regional Administration. OMAYA provides the Services only within the scope of the licences, approvals, registrations, exemptions, partnerships, or permissions available to it from time to time. Some Services may be provided through third-party partners, and some Services or features may be unavailable in certain jurisdictions or to certain users.\n\n## 2. Definitions\n\nIn these Terms, unless the context requires otherwise:\n\n- \"**Account**\" means the account you register with OMAYA to access the Services.\n- \"**Authorised User**\" means a person permitted to access or give instructions on an Account on behalf of the Account holder.\n- \"**Beneficial Owner**\" means a natural person who ultimately owns or controls a customer or on whose behalf a transaction is conducted.\n- \"**Broker**\" means a third-party foreign exchange broker with whom OMAYA has a partnership and in respect of whom OMAYA acts as a local agent (see Section 7).\n- \"**Digital Asset**\" means any digital representation of value that can be stored and transferred electronically, including cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin (BTC), stablecoins such as USDT (Tether), and any other virtual asset supported on the Platform from time to time.\n- \"**Exchange**\" means the service described in Section 6.1.\n- \"**Fiat**\" means government-issued currency that is legal tender in its country of issue.\n- \"**Forex Services**\" means the services described in Section 7.\n- \"**MoneyX**\" means the local payment transfer services described in Section 6.3.\n- \"**P2P Merchant**\" means a user approved by OMAYA to post advertisements and trade as a seller (and, where permitted, buyer) in the P2P market under OMAYA's merchant or verified-seller program.\n- \"**P2P Services**\" means the peer-to-peer trading services described in Section 8.\n- \"**Platform**\" means the OMAYA.io website, mobile application, and related systems through which the Services are provided.\n- \"**Self-Hosted Wallet**\" means an external Digital Asset wallet controlled by a user or third party and not hosted or controlled by OMAYA or another regulated virtual asset service provider.\n- \"**Services**\" means all products, features, and services made available by OMAYA, as described in these Terms.\n- \"**Stablecoin**\" means a Digital Asset designed or marketed to maintain a reference value relative to Fiat, another asset, or a basket of assets.\n- \"**Swap**\" means the crypto-to-crypto conversion service described in Section 6.2.\n- \"**Transaction**\" means any exchange, trade, conversion, transfer, deposit, withdrawal, or remittance carried out through the Services.\n- \"**Travel Rule**\" means legal, regulatory, or industry requirements to collect, transmit, verify, or retain originator and beneficiary information for virtual asset transfers.\n- \"**you**\" or \"**your**\" means the individual or entity using the Services. Where you act on behalf of an entity, you confirm you are authorised to bind that entity, and \"you\" refers to both you and that entity.\n\n## 3. Eligibility\n\n3.1. To use the Services, you must:\n\n(a) be at least **18 years old** and have full legal capacity to enter into a binding contract;  \n(b) not be a resident of, or located in, a jurisdiction where use of the Services is prohibited, or a jurisdiction subject to comprehensive sanctions or designated by the Financial Action Task Force (FATF) as high-risk and subject to a call for action;  \n(c) not be a person or entity subject to sanctions administered by the United Nations, the United States Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC), the European Union, the United Kingdom, the Central Bank of Somalia, or any other applicable authority, nor owned or controlled by, or acting on behalf of, any such person;  \n(d) not have been previously suspended or removed from the Services; and  \n(e) comply with all laws applicable to you in connection with your use of the Services.\n\n3.2. The Services are not offered where prohibited by law. We may restrict or refuse access to any person or in any jurisdiction at our discretion and in accordance with applicable law. You are solely responsible for ensuring that your use of the Services is lawful where you are located.\n\n3.3. You may not use another person's identity, or access the Services through tools intended to disguise your location or circumvent eligibility or geographic controls.\n\n## 4. Your Account\n\n4.1. **Registration.** To use most Services you must register an Account and provide accurate, current, and complete information. You agree to keep this information up to date.\n\n4.2. **One account.** Unless we approve otherwise in writing, you may hold only one Account and may use the Account only for your own benefit and not on behalf of any undisclosed third party.\n\n4.3. **Security.** You are responsible for safeguarding your Account credentials and for all activity that occurs under your Account. You must keep your password and any authentication methods confidential, enable available security features, and notify us immediately at support@omaya.io if you suspect unauthorised access. We are not liable for losses arising from your failure to keep your credentials secure.\n\n4.4. **Accuracy and cooperation.** You authorise us to rely on the instructions and information you provide. We may at any time require you to provide additional information or documentation, and you agree to cooperate promptly with such requests.\n\n4.5. **Corporate accounts.** Where the Account is held by a company, partnership, organisation, trust, foundation, association, or other legal entity, we may require documents and information to verify the entity, its business activity, ownership and control structure, directors, managers, Authorised Users, and Beneficial Owners, together with source of funds, source of wealth, and the purpose of the relationship.\n\n4.6. **Beneficial owners and controllers.** We may require identification and verification of Beneficial Owners, controlling persons, directors, senior managers, and any person who owns, controls, benefits from, or gives instructions in relation to an entity Account.\n\n4.7. **Authority to act.** We may require board resolutions, authorisation letters, powers of attorney, licences, constitutional documents, or other evidence that a person is authorised to open or operate a corporate Account. You confirm that you are duly authorised to act for and bind the entity, which is jointly and severally bound by these Terms.\n\n4.8. **Authorised Users.** A corporate Account holder is responsible for all acts, omissions, instructions, and activity of its Authorised Users, and we may act on instructions from Authorised Users in accordance with the permissions set for the Account.\n\n4.9. **Changes to ownership or control.** You must promptly notify us of any change in beneficial ownership, control, directors, Authorised Users, business activity, licensing status, sanctions status, or other information previously provided. We may refuse, suspend, restrict, or close a corporate Account where we cannot verify the entity, its Beneficial Owners, its source of funds, or its authority to use the Services, or where the entity is outside our risk appetite.\n\n## 5. Identity Verification, KYC, AML and Sanctions\n\n5.1. OMAYA is subject to anti-money laundering and counter-terrorism financing obligations and maintains a compliance program consistent with applicable Somali law (including the Anti-Money Laundering Law and the requirements of the Financial Reporting Center and the Central Bank of Somalia) and international standards.\n\n5.2. As a condition of using the Services, you agree to complete identity verification (\"**KYC**\") and to provide any information and documentation we request to verify your identity, source of funds, source of wealth, and the purpose of your Transactions. We use third-party identity verification and screening providers to perform these checks.\n\n5.3. We may, at our discretion and to the extent permitted or required by law: (a) refuse to open, suspend, restrict, or close an Account; (b) delay, refuse, freeze, reverse, or cancel any Transaction; (c) request further information or documentation; and (d) report activity to, and share information with, competent authorities, where we consider it necessary to comply with our legal obligations, to manage financial crime risk, or to protect OMAYA or others. Where the law prohibits us from disclosing the reason for such action (for example, where doing so would constitute unlawful \"tipping off\"), we may be unable to explain it to you.\n\n5.4. **Virtual asset transfer information and Travel Rule.** For Digital Asset transfers, we may collect, verify, store, transmit, and receive information about the originator, beneficiary, wallet owner, counterparty, and transaction purpose, as required by applicable law, the Travel Rule, payment partners, or our compliance procedures. We may share originator and beneficiary information with other virtual asset service providers, financial institutions, regulators, or law enforcement, and may delay, reject, freeze, return, or cancel a transfer where required information is missing, incomplete, inconsistent, or unacceptable to us.\n\n5.5. **Wallet verification and self-hosted wallets.** We may require you to verify that you own or control an external wallet address before allowing deposits, withdrawals, or transfers. Transfers to or from Self-Hosted Wallets may be subject to enhanced due diligence, ownership checks, limits, delays, or refusal, and we may decline to support a Self-Hosted Wallet where we consider the risk unacceptable.\n\n5.6. **Blockchain analytics and screening.** We may screen wallet addresses, transactions, and blockchain activity using internal tools and third-party analytics providers, and may reject, delay, freeze, return, or report transactions associated with sanctions, darknet markets, mixers, ransomware, scams, stolen funds, terrorist financing, or other activity outside our risk appetite.\n\n5.7. **Enhanced due diligence, PEPs and high-risk factors.** We may apply enhanced due diligence to any user, Account, transaction, wallet, counterparty, jurisdiction, or payment method we consider higher risk. High-risk factors include, without limitation, high-risk or sanctioned jurisdictions, FATF-listed jurisdictions, politically exposed persons, adverse media, unusual or high-volume transaction patterns, complex ownership structures, third-party payments, crypto-mixer exposure, and cross-border transfers. We may request additional documents and evidence, and may refuse onboarding, restrict features, lower limits, delay or reject transactions, or terminate the relationship where we determine the risk is unacceptable, even if the activity is not expressly prohibited by these Terms.\n\n5.8. **Biometric and liveness verification.** Our identity-verification providers may require a facial image or selfie, liveness detection, document authenticity checks, or related biometric verification to confirm your identity and prevent fraud. Such checks are carried out subject to our **Privacy Policy** and applicable law.\n\n5.9. Further detail is set out in our **AML/KYC Policy**.\n\n## 6. Our Services\n\n*In the Services described in this Section, OMAYA acts as principal or operator and is your service provider or counterparty. Different arrangements apply to Forex Services (Section 7), where OMAYA acts only as a local agent, and to P2P Services (Section 8), where OMAYA acts only as a facilitator.*\n\n6.1. **Exchange (Crypto ↔ Local Payment).** OMAYA enables you to buy supported Digital Assets (including BTC and USDT) using supported local payment methods, and to sell supported Digital Assets for payout to supported local payment methods, at the rates we quote at the time of the Transaction.\n\n6.2. **Crypto-to-Crypto Swap.** OMAYA enables you to convert one supported Digital Asset into another (a \"Swap\") at the rates we quote at the time of the Swap. Swap rates are indicative until the Swap is confirmed and may be sourced through third-party liquidity providers or exchanges (see Section 20). You are responsible for selecting the correct assets and networks; once confirmed, a Swap is generally final and irreversible.\n\n6.3. **MoneyX — Local Payment Transfers.** OMAYA enables you to move value between supported local payment providers, banks, mobile money services, e-wallets, and payment applications — for example, from one local wallet to another — subject to verification, limits, fees, availability, and applicable law. The supported channels are shown on the Platform and may be added, removed, suspended, or limited at any time.\n\n(a) **Correct details.** You are solely responsible for providing accurate payment details, including phone numbers, wallet and account numbers, account names, references, and beneficiary information. OMAYA is not responsible for losses, delays, or failed transfers caused by incorrect, incomplete, or incompatible details you provide.  \n(b) **Name matching and third-party payments.** We may require the sending or receiving account name to match the verified name on your Account, and may reject, delay, reverse, or hold any payment involving a third-party account, unmatched name, or unapproved payment source.  \n(c) **Provider delays and outages.** MoneyX depends on third-party banks, mobile money operators, payment processors, and telecom operators. OMAYA is not responsible for delays, outages, rejected transfers, provider errors, or settlement failures caused by these third parties.  \n(d) **Quotes and quote expiry.** Rates may be indicative until confirmed and may expire if payment is not completed in time, if market rates change, or if the transaction is subject to compliance review. We may requote, cancel, or reject a transaction where the original quote is no longer valid.  \n(e) **Failed, pending, reversed, or duplicate payments.** We may delay completion, request evidence, return funds where possible, deduct duplicate credits, or restrict the Account to correct an issue and manage risk. A screenshot, receipt, or notification does not guarantee that funds have been finally received and cleared.\n\n6.4. **Currency Exchange.** OMAYA provides currency exchange and conversion between supported currencies at the rates we quote at the time of the Transaction.\n\n6.5. **Remittance and Payments.** OMAYA provides remittance and payment services enabling you to send and receive funds through supported channels, subject to verification, limits, and applicable law.\n\n6.6. **Balances and Custody.**\n\n(a) Where the Services allow you to hold Fiat or Digital Asset balances, those balances are held by us for you. Holding a balance with OMAYA is not a bank deposit and is not insured or guaranteed by any deposit protection, investor compensation, or government guarantee scheme unless expressly required by applicable law. Unless we expressly agree otherwise in writing, balances do not earn interest.  \n(b) **Safeguarding.** We use reasonable administrative, technical, operational, and security measures designed to safeguard balances we hold. Where required by applicable law or our internal policies, we may hold client Fiat funds separately from our own operating funds.  \n(c) **Custody structure.** Digital Assets may be held in hot, warm, cold, omnibus, segregated, or third-party custodian wallets selected by us. Unless we expressly state otherwise, Digital Assets may be held in omnibus wallets together with assets of other users.  \n(d) **No unauthorised use.** Unless expressly disclosed to you and permitted by applicable law, we will not sell, lend, pledge, rehypothecate, or otherwise use your assets for our own trading, lending, investment, or speculative purposes.  \n(e) **Custody and insolvency risk.** Custody of Digital Assets involves operational and technological risks, including private-key compromise, cyber-attacks, wallet or network failure, smart-contract vulnerabilities, and third-party custodian failure.\n\n6.7. **Availability and changes.** We may add, modify, suspend, or discontinue any Service, feature, or supported asset, and may set or change limits at any time, acting reasonably and in accordance with applicable law.\n\n## 7. Forex Services — OMAYA as Local Agent\n\n**This Section governs OMAYA's role in connection with foreign exchange and contract-for-difference (\"CFD\") trading services provided by third-party Brokers.**\n\n7.1. **OMAYA's role is limited to that of a local agent.** In connection with the Forex Services, OMAYA acts **solely as a local agent and introducer** for one or more Brokers.\n\n7.2. **What OMAYA is not, and does not do.** In connection with the Forex Services, OMAYA is **not** the Broker and is **not** a party or counterparty to any trade.\n\n7.3. **Your trading relationship is with the Broker.** Your trading account, your trading agreement, and all trading activity are between **you and the Broker** and are governed exclusively by the Broker's own terms, agreements, policies, and risk disclosures.\n\n7.4. **No liability for the Broker.** To the maximum extent permitted by law, OMAYA is **not responsible or liable** for the acts, omissions, or performance of any Broker.\n\n7.5. **Funds handling.** Where OMAYA facilitates a transfer between you and a Broker, OMAYA acts only as a **local payment conduit**.\n\n7.6. **Risk.** Foreign exchange and CFD trading is highly speculative, involves substantial risk, and can result in the loss of all funds and, due to leverage, losses exceeding the amount you deposit. You should not trade unless you fully understand and can afford these risks. See our **Risk Disclosure Statement**.\n\n## 8. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Trading\n\n**In connection with P2P Services, OMAYA acts only as a facilitator and is not a party or counterparty to the trade between users.**\n\n8.1. **P2P Services.** Where OMAYA makes P2P Services available, you may buy or sell supported Digital Assets with other users using supported payment methods, subject to the limits, eligibility, fees, and procedures shown on the Platform.\n\n8.2. **OMAYA's role.** In P2P Services, OMAYA acts only as a platform provider, technology facilitator, and, where applicable, escrow or asset-locking facilitator.\n\n## 9. Orders, Pricing, Execution and Settlement\n\n9.1. **Quotes and pricing.** Prices, exchange rates, and quotes displayed on the Platform are indicative and may change rapidly.\n\n9.2. **Authorisation and finality.** **Transactions involving Digital Assets and blockchain transfers are generally irreversible and cannot be cancelled, reversed, or recovered once submitted.**\n\n## 10. Digital Assets: Forks, Airdrops, Migrations and Delisting\n\nOMAYA may decide whether and how to support forks, airdrops, upgrades, token swaps, migrations, or delistings.\n\n## 11. Deposits and Withdrawals\n\nYou may fund your Account and make withdrawals through the methods we make available, subject to verification, limits, fees, and applicable law.\n\n## 12. Security, Device Controls and Fraud Prevention\n\nWe may monitor and process security-related information to protect users and the Platform, and we may delay or block Transactions where we suspect fraud or scams.\n\n## 13. Fees, Charges, Set-Off and Negative Balances\n\nYou agree to pay all applicable fees, spreads, and charges for the Services, as published on the Platform or in our **Payment Policy**.\n\n## 14. Promotions, Rewards and Referral Controls\n\nPromotions are discretionary and may be subject to separate terms, eligibility rules, and anti-abuse controls.\n\n## 15. Risk Disclosure and No Advice\n\nOMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice. A full description of risks is set out in our **Risk Disclosure Statement**.\n\n## 16. Prohibited Uses and Restricted Activities\n\nYou must not use the Services to breach laws or sanctions, engage in financial crime, or commit fraud, manipulation, or other harmful activity.\n\n## 17. Suspension, Restriction, Closure, Account Deletion and Dormant Accounts\n\nWe may suspend or close Accounts to comply with law, manage risk, or address suspected fraud or breaches.\n\n## 18. Intellectual Property and Licence\n\nAll intellectual property rights in the Platform and the Services are owned by or licensed to OMAYA.\n\n## 19. Mobile Application Terms\n\nThe App is licensed, not sold, to you; additional app-store terms apply.\n\n## 20. Third-Party Providers, Partners and Links\n\nThe Services may rely on third parties; we are not responsible for third-party services except as expressly stated in these Terms.\n\n## 21. Privacy and Data Protection\n\nOur collection and use of personal data is described in our **Privacy Policy**.\n\n## 22. Electronic Communications and Notices\n\nYou consent to receiving communications from us electronically.\n\n## 23. Taxes and Information Reporting\n\nYou are responsible for determining and paying any taxes that apply to you.\n\n## 24. Disclaimers\n\nThe Services are provided **\"as is\" and \"as available\"** to the maximum extent permitted by law.\n\n## 25. Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, OMAYA’s liability is limited as described in these Terms.\n\n## 26. Indemnification\n\nYou agree to indemnify OMAYA for claims arising from your use or breach.\n\n## 27. Governing Law, Complaints and Dispute Resolution\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Somalia.\n\n## 28. Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may amend these Terms from time to time.\n\n## 29. General Provisions\n\nStandard contract provisions apply, including severability and force majeure.\n\n## 30. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- General and support: support@omaya.io  \n- Legal: legal@omaya.io  \n- Compliance: compliance@omaya.io\n\n---\n\n*These Terms of Service should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel familiar with the laws of Somalia and the jurisdictions in which OMAYA's customers are located before publication.*\n","OMAYA-Privacy-Policy-v1.2.md":"# Privacy Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.2\n\n---\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**, a private limited company incorporated under Company Law No. 18 of 26 December 2019 of the Federal Republic of Somalia (Registration No. LAG/UBI: 12029035324), with its registered office at Aaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia (\"**OMAYA**,\" \"**OMAYA EXCHANGE**,\" \"**OMAYA.io**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\"), collects, uses, shares, and protects your personal data when you use our website, mobile application, and services (the \"**Services**\").\n\nOMAYA is the **data controller** responsible for your personal data. This Privacy Policy should be read together with our **Terms of Service** and our **Cookie Policy**. If you do not agree with this Privacy Policy, you should not use the Services.\n\n**Applicable data-protection law.** We process personal data primarily in accordance with applicable Somali law, including the Data Protection Act, 2023 (Law No. 005) and any regulations or guidance issued by the Somalia Data Protection Authority, together with our obligations under Somali financial and anti-money-laundering law. Where you are located in another region, additional data-protection laws may also apply to you, as described in Section 15.\n\nIf you have any questions or wish to exercise your rights, contact us at **privacy@omaya.io**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Personal Data We Collect\n\nWe collect the following categories of personal data.\n\n### 1.1 Information you provide to us\n\n- **Identity and contact information:** full name, date and place of birth, nationality, residential address, email address, and phone number.\n- **Identity verification (KYC) information:** identity documents (such as passport, national identity card, or driving licence), proof of address, and related photographs or scans.\n- **Biometric and liveness data:** a facial image or selfie, liveness-check data, and document-authenticity data, collected through our identity-verification provider to confirm your identity and prevent fraud. These checks are used only for identity verification, fraud prevention, and compliance. Where biometric verification is required for KYC, refusing it may prevent us from opening or maintaining your Account or providing certain Services. Our verification provider may process this information on our behalf, and OMAYA generally receives verification results, risk indicators, and supporting records rather than raw biometric templates. Where we rely on your consent for biometric processing, we seek it separately at the point of verification (see Section 1.4).\n- **Financial and transaction information:** payment details (including, where you make card payments, limited payment-card information processed by our payment providers — we do not store full card details), bank and mobile-money account details, wallet addresses, transaction history, and information about your source of funds and source of wealth.\n- **Account and profile information:** username, account settings, and preferences.\n- **P2P information:** advertisements, order details, in-app chat messages, payment proofs, and dispute evidence. If you are a P2P Merchant, we may also collect additional verification information, security-deposit or reserve details, and performance metrics such as completion and release rates.\n- **Communications:** messages to our support team, complaints, and survey or feedback responses.\n- **Corporate account information:** entity details, directors, beneficial owners, authorised users, and supporting documents.\n- **Privacy choices and consent records:** records of your consents, permissions, opt-outs, and withdrawals, such as for marketing, cookies, location, and biometric processing.\n\n### 1.2 Information we collect automatically\n\n- **Device and technical information:** device and browser type, operating system, device identifiers, and app version.\n- **Network and location information:** IP address, approximate location, and, where you grant permission, more precise location.\n- **Usage information:** features and pages used, log data, and session and login activity.\n- **Security and fraud-prevention signals:** device fingerprint, risk signals, and behavioural patterns used to detect fraud and protect accounts.\n- **Diagnostics and notifications:** analytics, crash reports, diagnostics, performance and error logs, and, where you enable push notifications, device tokens and notification delivery information.\n- **Cookies and similar technologies:** as described in our **Cookie Policy**.\n\n### 1.3 Blockchain and transaction data\n\nDigital Asset transactions are recorded on public blockchains. We may collect and analyse wallet addresses and on-chain transaction data, including by using blockchain-analytics tools, for compliance, security, and fraud-prevention purposes.\n\n### 1.4 Information we receive from third parties\n\nWe may receive personal data about you from: identity-verification and screening providers (including **Sumsub**, which performs identity verification, biometric and document checks, and sanctions, PEP, and watchlist screening); sanctions, politically-exposed-person, and adverse-media data sources; blockchain-analytics providers; payment, banking, and mobile-money partners; third-party sign-in providers (where you choose to register or log in using them); our affiliates; and publicly available sources.\n\n## 2. How We Use Your Personal Data\n\nWe use your personal data to:\n\n- provide, operate, and maintain the Services and process your Transactions;\n- create, verify, and manage your Account, including identity verification and onboarding;\n- meet our anti-money-laundering and counter-terrorism-financing obligations, including KYC, sanctions and PEP screening, transaction monitoring, and the Travel Rule;\n- detect, prevent, and investigate fraud, scams, and security threats, and manage risk;\n- comply with our legal and regulatory obligations and respond to requests from regulators, the Financial Reporting Center, the Central Bank of Somalia, and other competent authorities;\n- secure the Platform and your Account;\n- provide customer support and handle complaints;\n- improve, personalise, and develop the Services;\n- send you service, transaction, security, and legal communications, and, where permitted, marketing communications; and\n- enforce our Terms of Service and protect our rights, property, and users.\n\n## 3. Legal Bases for Processing\n\nWhere data-protection law (such as the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation) applies, we rely on the following legal bases:\n\n- **Performance of a contract** — to provide the Services you request and operate your Account.\n- **Compliance with legal obligations** — including anti-money-laundering, counter-terrorism-financing, sanctions, tax, and record-keeping requirements.\n- **Legitimate interests** — including securing our Platform, preventing fraud, improving the Services, and direct marketing where permitted, balanced against your rights and interests.\n- **Consent** — for certain marketing, certain cookies, and where otherwise required; you may withdraw consent at any time.\n- **Biometric and special-category data** — we process biometric data (for identity verification) where it is necessary for compliance with our legal obligations and/or on the basis of your explicit consent, and on grounds of substantial public interest where applicable.\n\nThe table below maps our main processing purposes to their legal bases. Where more than one basis applies, we rely on each as relevant:\n\n| Purpose | Legal basis |\n|---|---|\n| Creating and operating your Account | Performance of a contract |\n| KYC, AML, sanctions and PEP screening | Legal obligation; substantial public interest; explicit consent where required (e.g., biometrics) |\n| Processing Transactions | Performance of a contract; legal obligation |\n| Fraud prevention and security | Legitimate interests; legal obligation |\n| Travel Rule compliance | Legal obligation |\n| Customer support | Performance of a contract; legitimate interests |\n| Marketing | Consent, or legitimate interests where permitted |\n| Improving the Services | Legitimate interests |\n| Legal claims and enforcement | Legitimate interests; legal obligation |\n\n## 4. How We Share Your Personal Data\n\n**We do not sell your personal data.** We may share it with:\n\n- **Service providers and processors** acting on our behalf under contract, including identity-verification and screening providers (such as Sumsub), hosting and IT providers, analytics and communications providers, and customer-support providers;\n- **Payment, banking, and mobile-money partners, liquidity providers, and cryptocurrency exchanges**, to process or route your Transactions;\n- **Partner foreign exchange Brokers**, where you use our Forex Services, to facilitate your onboarding, compliance vetting, and the settlement of local deposits and withdrawals;\n- **Blockchain-analytics and fraud-prevention providers**;\n- **Other virtual asset service providers and financial institutions**, where necessary to comply with the Travel Rule or to process a transfer. To comply with the Travel Rule, we may be required to transmit information such as the originator's name, account or wallet identifier, and address or identification number, together with the beneficiary's name and account or wallet identifier, to the counterparty provider;\n- **Regulators, the Financial Reporting Center, the Central Bank of Somalia, law enforcement, courts, and other authorities**, where required or permitted by law;\n- **Professional advisers**, such as legal, audit, and accounting advisers;\n- **Parties to a corporate transaction**, such as a merger, acquisition, or reorganisation; and\n- **Other parties with your consent** or at your direction.\n\nWe require our service providers to protect your personal data and to use it only for the purposes for which it is shared. For more information about how we handle law-enforcement and government requests, see our **Law Enforcement Request Guidelines**.\n\n## 5. Third-Party Sign-In and Platform Integrations\n\nWhere you choose to register or log in using a third-party sign-in provider, we receive certain information from that provider (such as your name, email address, and an account identifier), as permitted by your settings with that provider. Your use of any third-party sign-in or account is also governed by that provider's own terms and privacy policy. Where we use third-party platform services, we handle any personal data we receive in accordance with this Privacy Policy and the applicable requirements of those platforms.\n\n## 6. International Data Transfers\n\nWe are based in Somalia and may transfer and store personal data in Somalia and in other countries where we or our service providers operate. Our service providers — including our identity-verification provider, hosting and analytics providers, blockchain-analytics providers, and payment partners — may process personal data in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and other countries where they or their sub-processors operate. Where we transfer the personal data of individuals located in the EEA or the UK to a country that does not have an adequacy decision, we use appropriate safeguards — such as standard contractual clauses or the UK international data-transfer addendum — or rely on a permitted exception. You may contact us at **privacy@omaya.io** to request further information about the safeguards we use for international transfers.\n\n## 7. Automated Decision-Making and Profiling\n\nWe use automated systems and automated decision-making for fraud detection, transaction and sanctions screening, risk scoring, and compliance. These processes may result in a Transaction or Account being delayed, refused, restricted, or closed. Where a decision that produces legal or similarly significant effects is based solely on automated processing, you may request human review — except where the processing is necessary for entering into or performing a contract with you, is required for compliance with our legal obligations (such as anti-money-laundering requirements), or is based on your explicit consent.\n\n## 8. Marketing Communications\n\nService, transaction, security, and legal communications form part of the Services, and you may be unable to opt out of them while you hold an Account. We may also send marketing or promotional messages by email, SMS, messaging apps, or push notification where permitted. You can opt out of marketing communications at any time using the unsubscribe option or by contacting us; opting out will not affect service, transaction, security, or legal communications.\n\n## 9. Cookies and Similar Technologies\n\nWe use cookies and similar technologies to operate the Platform, remember your preferences, improve the Services, and support security and analytics. For details, and to manage your choices, please see our **Cookie Policy**.\n\n## 10. Data Retention\n\nWe keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy and to meet our legal, regulatory, and record-keeping obligations. Indicative retention periods are:\n\n- **Identity, KYC, and transaction records:** at least five (5) years after the end of your relationship with us or after the relevant Transaction, as required by anti-money-laundering and record-keeping rules.\n- **Compliance, screening, and suspicious-activity records:** at least five (5) years.\n- **Account and communications records:** for the duration of your relationship with us and a reasonable period afterward.\n- **Marketing data:** until you withdraw consent or object, or until it is no longer needed.\n- **Biometric and liveness records:** retained only for as long as necessary for identity verification, fraud prevention, AML/CFT compliance, legal claims, and audit, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law.\n- **Security, device, and fraud-prevention logs:** for the period necessary for security and fraud-prevention purposes.\n\nAfter the applicable period, we delete or anonymise your personal data, subject to copies that may remain in backups for a limited period until overwritten (see Section 13).\n\n## 11. Data Security\n\nWe maintain technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal data, including encryption, access controls, and monitoring. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. If we become aware of a personal-data breach, we will assess it promptly and, where required by applicable law (including the Data Protection Act, 2023), notify affected users and/or the competent authority.\n\n## 12. Your Privacy Rights\n\nThe following rights apply to the extent required by the data-protection law that applies to you, and may vary depending on where you live:\n\n- **Access** — to obtain confirmation of, and a copy of, the personal data we hold about you;\n- **Rectification** — to correct inaccurate or incomplete data;\n- **Erasure** — to request deletion of your data (the \"right to be forgotten\");\n- **Restriction** — to restrict our processing in certain circumstances;\n- **Data portability** — to receive certain data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format;\n- **Objection** — to object to processing based on legitimate interests and to direct marketing;\n- **Withdrawal of consent** — where processing is based on consent;\n- **Automated decisions** — not to be subject to solely automated decisions producing legal or similarly significant effects, subject to the exceptions in Section 7; and\n- **Complaint** — to lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority.\n\nThese rights are subject to limitations. In particular, we are required to retain certain records (such as KYC and transaction records) for anti-money-laundering, tax, and legal purposes, and may be unable to delete them even if you request erasure.\n\nTo exercise any of these rights, contact us at **privacy@omaya.io**. We may need to verify your identity before responding. We will respond within the time required by applicable law (for example, within one month under the GDPR, which may be extended for complex requests).\n\n## 13. Account Closure and Data Deletion\n\nYou may close your Account as described in our Terms of Service. You may also request deletion of your Account and personal data:\n\n- through the **in-app account-deletion option** in the OMAYA.io mobile application; or\n- through our **account-deletion page** at https://omaya.io/delete-account, which is also linked in the App and on our website.\n\nAccount closure and account deletion are different. Closure ends your access to the Services; deletion involves removing or deactivating personal data from our active systems. Following a deletion request, we will delete or anonymise your personal data, **except** for data we are required or permitted to retain for the periods set out in Section 10 (including KYC, transaction, compliance, tax, and legal records). Deletion may be delayed or refused where your Account has pending Transactions, remaining balances, unresolved disputes, investigations, or legal holds. Copies of deleted data may remain in our backups and disaster-recovery systems for a limited period until they are overwritten in the ordinary course. If those systems are ever restored, we apply controls designed to ensure that data you asked us to delete is not reinstated into our active systems and is re-deleted.\n\n## 14. Children's Privacy\n\nThe Services are intended only for individuals aged 18 or over. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 18. If we become aware that we have collected personal data from a person under 18, we will delete it.\n\n## 15. Region-Specific Information\n\n### 15.1 European Economic Area and United Kingdom\n\nIf you are located in the EEA or the UK, OMAYA is the data controller of your personal data; the legal bases on which we process it are set out in Section 3; your rights are set out in Section 12; and information about international transfers is in Section 6. You have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority (in the EEA) or with the Information Commissioner's Office (in the UK). Where required by applicable law, OMAYA will appoint an EU and/or UK representative and will publish the representative's contact details.\n\n### 15.2 California\n\nThis section applies only where the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended, applies to OMAYA and to your personal information. If you are a California resident, we collect the categories of personal information described in Section 1 (which may include identifiers, financial and commercial information, internet and device activity, geolocation, and sensitive personal information such as government identifiers and biometric information) for the purposes described in Section 2, and we use sensitive personal information only for permitted purposes such as identity verification, security, and compliance. **We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.** You have the right to know about, access, delete, and correct your personal information, to limit the use of sensitive personal information, to opt out of any sale or sharing, and not to be discriminated against for exercising your rights; you may use an authorised agent to make a request, and we may verify your identity before responding. Because we do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising, this is not a sale or share opt-out; however, where required by applicable law, we honour Global Privacy Control and similar opt-out preference signals as a request to disable non-essential cookies (see our **Cookie Policy**). To exercise these rights, contact us at **privacy@omaya.io**.\n\n### 15.3 Other regions\n\nYou may have additional rights under the data-protection laws that apply where you live. Please contact us to find out more.\n\n## 16. Changes to This Privacy Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version on the Platform and update the \"Last Updated\" date, and where the changes are material we will take reasonable steps to notify you. Your continued use of the Services after the changes take effect indicates your acknowledgement of the updated Privacy Policy.\n\n## 17. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\nOMAYA has appointed a privacy contact responsible for handling privacy and data-protection requests.\n\n- Privacy and data-protection enquiries and requests: **privacy@omaya.io**\n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n","OMAYA-Cookie-Policy-v1.1.md":"# Cookie Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis Cookie Policy explains how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\") uses cookies and similar technologies on our website and mobile application (the \"**Platform**\"). It should be read together with our **Privacy Policy**, which explains how we handle personal data more generally.\n\nWe use strictly necessary cookies to operate the Platform and keep it secure. Where required by law, we will ask for your consent before setting functional, analytics, performance, or marketing cookies, and you can change or withdraw your choices at any time.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Are Cookies and Similar Technologies?\n\nCookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. We also use similar technologies, including:\n\n- **Pixels and web beacons** — small pieces of code that help us understand activity on the Platform;\n- **Local storage** — data stored by your browser or app to remember information between sessions;\n- **Software development kits (SDKs)** — code in our mobile app that supports functionality, analytics, and security; and\n- **Device identifiers** — identifiers associated with your device, used mainly in the app.\n\nIn this Policy, we refer to all of these as \"**cookies**.\"\n\n## 2. How We Use Cookies\n\nWe use cookies for the following purposes:\n\n| Category | Purpose | Consent |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Strictly necessary** | Security, authentication, fraud prevention, session management, and load balancing. These are required for the Platform to work and for keeping your account secure. | Always active; cannot be switched off |\n| **Functional** | Remembering your preferences and settings, such as language and display choices. | Set with consent where required |\n| **Analytics / performance** | Understanding how the Platform is used, measuring performance, and diagnosing errors so we can improve the Services. | Set with consent where required |\n| **Marketing** | Measuring and improving the effectiveness of our own marketing and campaigns — for example, understanding whether a visit led to a sign-up. | Set only with your consent |\n\nWe do not use cookies to sell your personal information.\n\nThe specific cookies and similar technologies we use are listed and kept up to date in our cookie settings tool. The following table is illustrative of the types of cookies we use; the live list may differ:\n\n| Cookie / technology | Provider | Category | Purpose | Duration |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Session / authentication token | OMAYA.io | Strictly necessary | Login and session security | Session |\n| Language and display preference | OMAYA.io | Functional | Remember your settings | Up to 12 months |\n| Analytics identifier | Analytics provider | Analytics / performance | Measure website and app usage | Up to 13 months |\n| Fraud / device identifier | Security provider | Strictly necessary (security) | Fraud prevention and account security | 12–24 months |\n\nThe specific cookies, SDKs, and similar technologies we use may change over time, and we will keep the current list in our cookie banner or settings tool.\n\n## 3. First-Party and Third-Party Cookies\n\nSome cookies are set by us (\"first-party cookies\"). Others are set by third parties that provide services on the Platform (\"third-party cookies\"), such as analytics providers, third-party sign-in providers (where you choose to register or log in using them), and security and fraud-prevention providers. These third parties may process information in accordance with their own privacy and cookie policies, which we encourage you to review. Third-party cookies may also be set by embedded financial tools, market-data or charting providers, and our cloud-infrastructure providers, where these are used to deliver real-time trading functionality and keep the Platform available. Accepting certain third-party cookies may involve the international transfer of information such as your IP address and device identifiers; we apply the safeguards described in Section 6 of our **Privacy Policy**.\n\n## 4. Cookies in Our Mobile App\n\nOur mobile application uses SDKs, local storage, and device identifiers to support core functionality, security and fraud prevention, analytics, and, where you consent, marketing measurement. You can manage many of these technologies through your device settings — for example, by resetting or limiting your device's advertising identifier or adjusting app permissions. The SDKs in our app may include analytics and crash-reporting tools, third-party sign-in (such as Google and Apple Sign-In), our identity-verification provider's SDK (Sumsub), push-notification and device-intelligence or fraud-prevention tools, and, where used, marketing-attribution tools. The current list of SDKs and the data they collect is reflected in our app-store privacy disclosures and our cookie settings tool.\n\n## 5. How Long Cookies Last\n\n- **Session cookies** are temporary and are deleted when you close your browser or app.\n- **Persistent cookies** remain on your device for a set period or until you delete them, so that we can recognise you on a return visit.\n\n## 6. Your Choices and How to Manage Cookies\n\nYou can control cookies in several ways:\n\n- **Cookie settings.** Our cookie banner and settings tool let you **accept all** non-essential cookies, **reject all** non-essential cookies, or **manage your choices by category**, and change or withdraw your consent at any time. You can manage your cookie choices at https://omaya.io/cookie-settings.\n- **Browser settings.** Most browsers let you block or delete cookies and notify you when a cookie is set. Refer to your browser's help pages for instructions.\n- **Device settings.** On mobile devices, you can reset or limit your advertising identifier and manage app permissions.\n- **Analytics and marketing opt-outs.** You can decline analytics and marketing cookies through our cookie settings, where available.\n\nPlease note that if you block strictly necessary cookies, parts of the Platform may not function properly, and we may be unable to keep your account secure.\n\n**Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.** Some browsers and devices send opt-out preference signals such as Global Privacy Control (GPC) or \"Do Not Track\" (DNT). Where required by applicable law, we treat a GPC signal as a valid request to disable non-essential (analytics and marketing) cookies. We do not sell your personal information or share it for cross-context behavioural advertising, and if our practices change we will honour applicable opt-out preference signals as required by law. You can also manage non-essential cookies using the controls above.\n\n## 7. Consent\n\nWhere required by applicable law (including in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom), we set non-essential cookies only with your consent, which we request through our cookie banner or settings tool. You can withdraw or change your consent at any time using those settings. Strictly necessary cookies do not require consent because they are essential to provide the Services and to protect security. We may keep records of your cookie choices, consent, refusal, and withdrawal to demonstrate compliance and respect your preferences, and you can request a copy of your cookie-consent record by contacting us at **privacy@omaya.io**.\n\n## 8. Changes to This Cookie Policy\n\nWe may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version on the Platform and update the \"Last Updated\" date. Where the changes are material, we will take reasonable steps to notify you.\n\n## 9. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Privacy and data-protection enquiries: **privacy@omaya.io**\n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This Cookie Policy should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel, and the categories above should be confirmed against the cookies and similar technologies actually used on the OMAYA.io website and app. The specific cookies in use should be listed and kept up to date in the cookie banner or settings tool on the Platform.*\n","OMAYA-AML-KYC-Policy-v1.1.md":"# AML/KYC Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis AML/KYC Policy describes how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\") prevents money laundering, terrorism financing, and other financial crime, and how we verify the identity of our customers. It is a public summary of OMAYA's internal Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing (AML/CFT) Policies and Procedures and forms part of our **Terms of Service**. It applies to all users of our website, mobile application, and services (the \"**Services**\").\n\nBecause financial crime controls must remain effective, this Policy describes our approach at a general level and does not disclose the internal thresholds, scoring rules, detection scenarios, or procedures that would undermine those controls.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Our Commitment\n\nOMAYA has **zero tolerance** for money laundering, terrorism financing, proliferation financing, sanctions evasion, fraud, and other financial crime. We are committed to operating with integrity and in full compliance with applicable law, and we apply a **risk-based approach** to identifying, assessing, mitigating, and managing these risks.\n\n## 2. Regulatory Status and Framework\n\nOMAYA holds a Commercial Licence issued by the Ministry of Commerce, a licence from the Central Bank of Somalia, and a licence from the Banadir Regional Administration.\n\nOur AML/CFT program is designed to comply with applicable **Somali law**, and we align our program with recognised **international standards**, including the recommendations of the Financial Action Task Force (FATF).\n\n## 3. Governance and Oversight\n\n- our **Board of Directors** has ultimate oversight and approves our AML/CFT policy;\n- we appoint a **Money Laundering Reporting Officer (MLRO)**; and\n- we operate a \"**three lines of defence**\" model.\n\n## 4. Risk-Based Approach and Customer Risk Rating\n\nWe classify customers and relationships into risk categories (for example, **low, standard, medium, high, or prohibited**) based on factors including customer type, geography, product use, transaction behaviour, sanctions and PEP exposure, source of funds and source of wealth, and delivery channel.\n\n## 5. Customer Due Diligence (KYC)\n\nDepending on risk, we apply **Simplified**, **Standard**, or **Enhanced** due diligence.\n\nAs part of KYC, we may require:\n\n- **Identity information**\n- **Identity documents**\n- **Verification checks** (document-authenticity, facial-image, liveness checks)\n- **Purpose and activity information**\n- **Source of funds and source of wealth** information\n\n## 6. Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD)\n\nWe apply EDD to higher-risk customers and activity.\n\n## 7. Sanctions Compliance\n\nWe screen customers and transactions against applicable sanctions lists and may freeze assets or block transactions where required.\n\n## 8. Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs)\n\nWe screen for PEPs and apply EDD and senior-management approval where relevant.\n\n## 9. Transaction Monitoring\n\nWe monitor activity to detect unusual transactions and potential financial crime and may reject, delay, or investigate transactions as needed.\n\n## 10. Digital Asset and Crypto Compliance\n\nWe use **blockchain-analytics tools** to screen wallet addresses and transactions, and we may apply controls to transfers involving **self-hosted wallets** and comply with **Travel Rule** requirements.\n\n## 11. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Controls\n\nWe apply additional controls to P2P trading and may monitor P2P chat and evidence for compliance and fraud purposes.\n\n## 12. Reliance on Third Parties and Partner Due Diligence\n\nWe perform risk-based due diligence on partners (payment providers, banks, brokers, and other service providers).\n\n## 13. Suspicious Activity and Regulatory Reporting\n\nWhere required, we report suspicious activity to the **Financial Reporting Center (FRC)** and cooperate with authorities. We may be legally prohibited from informing you of reports or investigations (\"tipping off\").\n\n## 14. Prohibited Customers and Activities\n\nWe do not establish or maintain relationships with sanctioned persons, anonymous customers, shell banks, or customers who refuse required information.\n\n## 15. Record-Keeping\n\nWe retain records for the periods required by applicable law (generally **at least five (5) years**).\n\n## 16. Account Restrictions, Refusal, and Closure\n\nWe may refuse onboarding, restrict features, delay or freeze transactions, or close accounts to comply with law and manage risk.\n\n## 17. Your Responsibilities\n\nYou must provide accurate information, complete verification, use payment accounts in your own name (unless approved otherwise), and cooperate with compliance checks.\n\n## 18. Program Governance, Training and Review\n\nWe train relevant personnel, apply controls, and test and review our program periodically.\n\n## 19. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this AML/KYC Policy from time to time.\n\n## 20. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Compliance and AML/KYC enquiries: **compliance@omaya.io**  \n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This public AML/KYC Policy is a summary and should be reviewed by OMAYA's MLRO and qualified legal counsel before publication.*\n","OMAYA-Risk-Disclosure-Statement-v1.1.md":"# Risk Disclosure Statement\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis Risk Disclosure Statement describes some of the risks of using the services of **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\"). It forms part of our **Terms of Service** and should be read together with them. It applies to all of our services, including our digital asset Exchange, crypto-to-crypto Swap, MoneyX local payment transfers, peer-to-peer (P2P) trading, foreign exchange, and remittance and payment services (the \"**Services**\").\n\n> **Important — please read carefully. Digital assets are high-risk.**\n> - **You could lose all of the money you use to buy, sell, hold, swap, or transfer digital assets.** Digital assets and balances held with OMAYA are generally **not** protected by any deposit-insurance, investor-compensation, financial-ombudsman, or chargeback scheme.\n> - Trading foreign exchange is also high-risk, and because of leverage you can lose **more than you deposit**.\n> - **Only use funds you can afford to lose** — never borrowed money, or money you need for living expenses, business operations, or other obligations.\n> - **OMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice.** All decisions are yours alone.\n> - This Statement does **not** describe every risk. You are responsible for understanding the Services before using them, and for seeking independent professional advice where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n## 1. No Advice and No Guarantee\n\nOMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice, and does not assess whether any product or transaction is suitable or appropriate for you. No content, price, rate, tool, ranking, or feature on the Platform is a recommendation, solicitation, or assurance of any outcome, and any articles, prices, calculators, or educational materials are **informational only**. We do not guarantee any profit, return, value, or result. **Past performance is not a reliable indicator of future results.** You are solely responsible for your own decisions and should obtain independent professional advice where appropriate.\n\n## 2. You May Lose Your Money\n\nThe value of digital assets and currencies can fall as well as rise, sometimes sharply and without warning, and you may lose some or all of the funds involved. You should assess your own financial situation, experience, and risk tolerance before using the Services.\n\n## 3. Do Not Use Borrowed or Essential Funds\n\nYou should not borrow money, or use emergency funds, customer funds, business operating funds, or funds you need for living expenses, to trade or hold digital assets or to trade foreign exchange. These activities can result in losses that exceed the funds you commit to them.\n\n## 4. Risks of Digital Assets (Cryptocurrency)\n\n- **Volatility.** Digital asset prices can be extremely volatile and can change dramatically in a short time, including to zero.\n- **Liquidity.** Markets can become illiquid, making it difficult or impossible to buy, sell, or convert an asset at the price or time you want.\n- **Irreversibility and wrong network.** Blockchain transactions are generally **final and cannot be reversed, cancelled, or recovered**. Sending assets to a wrong or incompatible address — or through an **unsupported or incorrect network** (for example, confusing networks such as TRC20, ERC20, BEP20, or others for the same asset) — or sending **unsupported tokens**, can result in **permanent loss**, and OMAYA may be unable or unwilling to recover them.\n- **Technology and network risk.** Networks may experience congestion, delays, forks, reorganisations, or attacks (including \"51%\" attacks), and **smart contracts and protocols may contain bugs or be exploited**, including hacks, liquidity-pool drains, and protocol failures.\n- **Network fees.** Blockchain network fees can rise suddenly and unpredictably and may reduce the final amount you receive.\n- **Market integrity.** Digital asset markets are relatively new and may be affected by **market manipulation, wash trading, spoofing, pump-and-dump activity, insider dealing, fake volume, social-media hype, low liquidity, and conflicts of interest** among issuers, exchanges, liquidity providers, or other participants.\n- **Issuer or project failure.** A digital asset may lose value, including to zero, because the issuer, protocol, or project **fails, is hacked, is abandoned, is fraudulent (for example, a \"rug pull\"), becomes insolvent, loses liquidity or its community, suffers a smart-contract failure, or becomes subject to regulatory action**.\n- **Security.** Digital assets are a target for theft, hacking, fraud, and key compromise. Loss of credentials, private keys, or recovery phrases can cause permanent loss of access.\n\n## 5. Custody and Insolvency Risk\n\nWhere OMAYA holds Fiat or digital assets for you, custody may involve hot, warm, cold, omnibus, segregated, or third-party custodian wallets, and your assets may be held together with those of other users. Custody involves operational, legal, insolvency, and third-party risks. **If OMAYA, or a relevant custodian, bank, payment provider, or liquidity provider, becomes insolvent or subject to legal process, access to your assets may be delayed, restricted, or affected, and the legal treatment of your assets may depend on applicable law and the custody structure used.** Balances held with OMAYA are not bank deposits and are not covered by any deposit-protection scheme unless required by law.\n\n## 6. Stablecoin Risks\n\nStablecoins (such as USDT) are digital assets and are **not** the same as cash or bank deposits. A stablecoin may **lose its peg** and trade above or below its reference value, become illiquid, or be suspended. Stablecoins depend on their issuer, reserves, redemption arrangements, and regulatory status, and we do not guarantee that any stablecoin is fully backed, redeemable, or equal to any currency. Issuers or network participants may **freeze, blacklist, burn, reissue, or refuse to redeem** stablecoins. You are responsible for selecting the correct network when transferring a stablecoin.\n\n## 7. Forks, Delisting, and Restricted or Unsupported Assets\n\nDigital asset networks may undergo **forks, airdrops, upgrades, token migrations, or redenominations**, and OMAYA may decide **not** to support any of them or any resulting new token. OMAYA may also **suspend, delist, or cease supporting** an asset — including abruptly, for legal, regulatory, liquidity, security, or risk reasons — in which case you may **lose access, be unable to trade or withdraw an asset, be required to withdraw it before a deadline, or have to liquidate a position at an unfavourable price**. Some assets, networks, or privacy-enhancing technologies may be **restricted or unsupported** for legal, compliance, sanctions, or AML/CFT reasons, which can affect your ability to deposit, withdraw, swap, or hold them.\n\n## 8. Risks of Crypto-to-Crypto Swaps\n\nExchange rates and estimated outputs for Swaps may be based on **third-party liquidity providers** and can change rapidly. A quote may be **delayed, unavailable, rejected, re-priced, or cancelled** because of market movement, liquidity-provider error, network fees, slippage, or compliance review, and a displayed rate **may not be the final executed rate**. Once confirmed, a Swap is generally **final and irreversible**, and you are responsible for selecting the correct assets and networks.\n\n## 9. Foreign Exchange (Forex) and Leverage Risks\n\nForeign exchange and contract-for-difference (\"CFD\") trading is **highly speculative and carries a high risk of loss**. It is not suitable for everyone.\n\n- **Leverage magnifies both gains and losses.** Because of leverage, you can **lose more than the amount you deposit**.\n- **Margin calls and liquidation.** Positions may be closed out automatically, and you may be required to provide additional funds at short notice.\n- **Execution risk.** During volatile markets, news events, low liquidity, market gaps, or \"flash crashes,\" orders may be executed at a **worse price than expected (slippage)**, spreads may **widen**, platforms may **requote or reject orders**, execution may be **delayed**, and stop-loss orders are **not guaranteed** unless the Broker expressly offers a guaranteed-stop product. Extreme, instantaneous volatility can also make it impossible to execute or close positions in time.\n- **Automated trading.** If you use automated trading systems, expert advisors (EAs), trading signals, or platforms such as MT4 or MT5 with a Broker, OMAYA is **not responsible** for losses caused by such systems, including runaway algorithms, signal failures, configuration errors, or latency and execution delays.\n- **Broker insolvency and protections.** Negative-balance protection and similar safeguards depend on the **Broker's rules and jurisdiction** and may not apply to you, and a Broker may become insolvent.\n- **OMAYA's limited role.** OMAYA acts **only as a local agent** for third-party Brokers. OMAYA is **not** the Broker, is **not** a party or counterparty to any trade, and does not operate the trading platform, execute trades, or hold your trading capital once it has been transferred to the Broker. Your trading relationship is **with the Broker** and is governed by the Broker's own terms and risk disclosures, which you should read before trading. OMAYA is not responsible or liable for the Broker or for any trading loss. See Section 7 of our **Terms of Service**.\n\n## 10. MoneyX, Remittance, and Local Payment Risks\n\n- Payments depend on third-party banks, mobile money operators, and payment providers, which may experience **delays, outages, or failures** outside our control.\n- You are responsible for providing **correct payment details**; incorrect or mismatched details can cause loss, delay, or failed transfers, and a completed transfer may be impossible to reverse.\n- A payment may be **delayed, held, refused, reversed, or refunded** for compliance, fraud, or operational reasons, and a refund may be made at the prevailing exchange rate, which can differ from the original rate.\n\n## 11. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Trading Risks\n\nIn P2P trading, you deal **directly with other users**. OMAYA acts only as a facilitator and is **not** the buyer, seller, counterparty, or guarantor.\n\n- A counterparty may fail to pay, fail to release assets, submit **false or forged payment proof**, or attempt fraud, and a payment may later be **reversed or charged back** even after assets are released.\n- A **P2P Merchant, verified-seller badge, rating, or completion rate does not guarantee** that a counterparty is trustworthy or risk-free. You must still verify that payment has actually been received, use only approved payment methods, and avoid off-platform settlement.\n- **External account-freeze risk.** If you receive funds from a counterparty whose funds are linked to fraud or are under investigation, **your own external bank or mobile money accounts may be frozen or restricted by banks or authorities**. OMAYA is not responsible for actions taken by external institutions or authorities against your accounts.\n- OMAYA's dispute review is an operational process, not a court or arbitration, and we may be unable to resolve every dispute or recover your funds. Dealing off-platform, or with anyone impersonating OMAYA, greatly increases the risk of fraud and loss.\n\n## 12. Compliance Holds, Sanctions, and Account Restrictions\n\nTo meet our legal obligations, your transactions or Account may be **delayed, refused, frozen, returned, restricted, reversed, closed, or reported** as a result of KYC, AML/CFT, sanctions, fraud, blockchain-analytics, Travel Rule, wallet-ownership, or counterparty checks, or in response to law-enforcement requests, court orders, or regulatory obligations. Transfers to or from **self-hosted wallets** may involve higher risk and additional checks, limits, delays, or refusal, because we may be unable to verify the wallet owner, source of funds, or transaction purpose. **We may be legally prohibited from telling you the reason for, or even the existence of, a delay, freeze, refusal, or report.**\n\n## 13. Platform and Operational Risks\n\nThe Platform may be **unavailable or interrupted** due to scheduled or emergency maintenance, upgrades, technical failures, third-party failures, or events beyond our control, and you may be unable to access your Account or complete transactions during such periods. Platform data may occasionally contain **errors** — including a wrong rate, stale prices, a decimal error, a duplicate credit, an incorrect balance display, an app calculation error, or a liquidity-provider error — and, where permitted by our Terms of Service and applicable law, we may **correct, cancel, reverse, or re-price** affected transactions. Events beyond our reasonable control — including **war, civil unrest, government action, regulatory change, power, telecom, or internet outages, cyber-attacks, blockchain failures, and natural disasters** — may also affect the Services.\n\n## 14. Security, Fraud, and Scam Risks\n\n- You are responsible for **safeguarding your Account**, credentials, devices, two-factor methods, and recovery information. Unauthorised access can lead to irreversible loss.\n- Be alert to **phishing, social engineering, and impersonation**. **OMAYA staff will never ask you for your password, full one-time passcodes or 2FA codes, recovery or seed phrases, or private keys, and will never ask you to move funds to a \"safe\" account.** Treat any such request as fraudulent.\n- **Mobile and app risk.** Using a compromised, rooted, or jailbroken device, or installing **fake or impersonating apps**, increases the risk of loss. Only use the official OMAYA.io app.\n- **Impersonation on social media.** Be cautious of fake OMAYA accounts or \"support\" agents on Telegram, WhatsApp, Facebook, TikTok, or other platforms.\n- Be cautious of **investment, romance, \"guaranteed-return,\" fake-broker, and giveaway scams**. If an opportunity sounds too good to be true, it almost certainly is. Funds sent to a scammer are usually **impossible to recover**.\n\n## 15. Regulatory and Legal Risks\n\nThe legal and regulatory treatment of digital assets and related services varies between jurisdictions and **may change**, sometimes suddenly, which can affect the availability, value, or legality of the Services or of particular assets. The Services may not be available, or may be restricted, in some jurisdictions. **You are responsible for ensuring that your use of the Services is lawful where you are located.**\n\n## 16. No Insurance, Compensation, or Ombudsman\n\nDigital assets and balances held with OMAYA are **not** bank deposits and are generally **not** protected by any deposit-insurance, investor-compensation, or government guarantee scheme. For certain digital asset transactions, you may also have **no access to a financial ombudsman, dispute scheme, or chargeback mechanism**. You should not assume that the protections available for traditional bank or card payments apply.\n\n## 17. Tax Risks\n\nYou are solely responsible for determining, reporting, and paying any taxes that apply to your use of the Services and your transactions. Tax treatment can be complex and may change, and your transaction history may be **incomplete** if you also transact outside OMAYA. You should consult a qualified tax adviser.\n\n## 18. Third-Party and Partner Risks\n\nThe Services rely on third parties, including liquidity providers, cryptocurrency exchanges, foreign exchange brokers, banks, mobile money providers, payment processors, and other providers. We do not control these third parties and are not responsible for their acts, omissions, delays, failures, or solvency, except as expressly stated in our Terms of Service.\n\n## 19. Acknowledgement\n\nBy using the Services, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Risk Disclosure Statement, that you understand the Services involve significant risk, and that you accept those risks. This Statement does not limit any other risk warnings or terms in our **Terms of Service** or other policies.\n\n## 20. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This Risk Disclosure Statement should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication and confirmed against the specific Services and assets OMAYA offers. It is not a substitute for independent financial, legal, or tax advice to customers.*\n","OMAYA-Law-Enforcement-Request-Guidelines-v1.1.md":"# Law Enforcement Request Guidelines\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThese Guidelines explain how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\") responds to requests from law enforcement, regulatory, and other government authorities (\"**Authorities**\") for customer information, the preservation of records, and the freezing or restriction of accounts or assets.\n\nThey are intended as practical guidance for Authorities and to inform our users. They are **not legal advice**, do not form part of any contract, and do **not** expand, limit, or waive any rights, obligations, defences, or objections available to OMAYA, our users, or any other person under applicable law.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose and Scope\n\nThese Guidelines apply to requests directed to OMAYA that relate to our Services, including requests for:\n\n- customer or account information;\n- the preservation of records;\n- the freezing, blocking, or restriction of accounts, transactions, or assets; and\n- other lawful assistance in connection with an investigation or legal proceeding.\n\n## 2. Governing Law and Cooperation with Authorities\n\nOMAYA is incorporated in the Federal Republic of Somalia and handles requests in accordance with applicable Somali law and our legal obligations. We cooperate with the **Financial Reporting Center (FRC)**, the **Central Bank of Somalia**, Somali law enforcement, courts, and other competent Somali Authorities. We may also respond to requests from foreign Authorities where there is a proper and lawful basis to do so (see Section 14). We will only disclose information, or take action, where we are permitted or required to do so by applicable law and valid legal process.\n\nLegal process should be served **directly on OMAYA** at our Mogadishu headquarters or through the contact channel in Section 17, and **not** on our cloud, hosting, or other infrastructure providers. Customer data is encrypted at rest, and we will contest or seek to redirect any request for customer data that is served on an underlying infrastructure provider rather than on OMAYA.\n\n## 3. How to Submit a Request\n\nRequests should be submitted by an authorised official to **lawenforcement@omaya.io**.\n\nTo allow us to identify the relevant records and respond, a request should:\n\n- be made on **official letterhead**, signed by an authorised official, and sent from an **official government email domain**;\n- identify the **issuing Authority** and the **name, title, and contact details** of the requesting official;\n- state the **legal basis and authority** for the request and any case or reference number;\n- specify the **information sought** and the **time period** to which it relates; and\n- identify the customer or account as precisely as possible — for example, by account email address, customer name, OMAYA account identifier, transaction reference, or wallet address.\n\nRequests that are vague, overly broad, or that do not identify a specific customer, account, or transaction may be declined or returned for clarification.\n\n**Response times.** We aim to acknowledge receipt of routine requests within **5 business days**. Full production of records typically takes **30 to 45 days**, depending on the volume and complexity of the request and the legal process involved. Emergency requests are handled on an expedited basis (see Section 6).\n\n## 4. Valid Legal Process Required\n\nWe require **valid legal process** appropriate to the request. Different categories of information or action may require different levels of legal process, and more sensitive information or actions (such as the disclosure of detailed records, the content of communications, or the freezing or seizure of assets) generally require a court order, warrant, or directive from a competent Authority. We review each request for **validity, legal sufficiency, and specificity**, and we may **object to, narrow, seek to modify, or decline** a request that is improper, overbroad, defective, or not supported by adequate legal authority.\n\n## 5. Categories of Records\n\nSubject to applicable law, valid legal process, and what we actually hold, the information we may be able to provide includes:\n\n- **subscriber and identity information** (such as name, date of birth, and contact details collected at registration);\n- **identity-verification (KYC) records**;\n- **account information** (such as account status and history);\n- **transaction records** (such as deposits, withdrawals, exchanges, swaps, transfers, and associated wallet addresses);\n- **device, IP, and login records**; and\n- **communications and P2P records** held by us, such as support correspondence and P2P dispute evidence.\n\nWe provide only the information we hold and that the legal process lawfully requires. The personal data we collect is described in our **Privacy Policy**.\n\n**Partner broker records.** Where OMAYA acts as a local agent for a third-party foreign exchange Broker, OMAYA does **not** hold and **cannot produce** that Broker's internal trading records — including trading-ledger data, order and execution records, margin-call histories, or MT4/MT5 terminal or Expert Advisor (EA) logs. Such records are held by the Broker, and Authorities must direct separate legal process to the relevant Broker entity in its own jurisdiction.\n\n**Detailed technical logs.** We provide standard transaction histories (such as deposits, withdrawals, exchanges, swaps, transfers, and final executions on our own Platform). Raw server-level logs, detailed event logs, or similar technical data that we hold may require a specific and narrowly framed request, may take additional time to extract, and may be subject to the cost reimbursement described in Section 12.\n\n## 6. Emergency Disclosure Requests\n\nWhere a request involves an **imminent risk of death or serious physical harm**, we operate an expedited process. An emergency request should be clearly marked as such, sent to **lawenforcement@omaya.io**, and include a good-faith explanation of the emergency, the harm at risk, and how the requested information will help prevent it. Where permitted by applicable law, we may voluntarily disclose information to an Authority if we believe in good faith that doing so is necessary to prevent such harm.\n\n## 7. Preservation Requests\n\nOn receipt of a valid preservation request, we will take reasonable steps to **preserve relevant records that we hold** for a period of **90 days**, which may be extended once on a further valid request, pending service of appropriate legal process. A preservation request does not by itself require us to disclose any information.\n\n## 8. Asset Freezing, Blocking, and Seizure\n\nWhere required by applicable law, a court order, or a directive from a competent Authority, and to meet our sanctions and AML/CFT obligations, we may **freeze, block, restrict, or decline to process** accounts, transactions, or assets, and report the matter. The treatment and availability of frozen or restricted assets is subject to applicable law and the relevant legal process.\n\nWe distinguish between a **freeze or blocking order**, which locks or restricts an account or assets on the OMAYA Platform, and a **forfeiture or seizure order**, which requires the transfer of assets out of OMAYA's control. We will act on a valid freeze order to lock or restrict assets, but we will **only transfer digital assets to a government-designated wallet, or otherwise release assets to an Authority, on receipt of a final, enforceable forfeiture or seizure order from a competent court** — not on the basis of a preliminary or investigative freeze request.\n\n## 9. Notice to Account Holders\n\nOur general approach is to be transparent with our users. We may **notify affected users** of a request for their information so that they may seek to protect their interests, **unless** we are prohibited from doing so by law, a court order, or a non-disclosure or \"tipping-off\" obligation, or where we believe in good faith that notice would be counterproductive — for example, where it could endanger a person, enable the destruction of evidence, or harm an investigation. **Where we are legally prohibited from giving notice, we will not do so, and we may be unable to confirm whether a request exists.**\n\nWe expect a non-disclosure or gag order to specify a **defined expiration date** (for example, 90 to 180 days). Where a non-disclosure order has no expiry or is of indefinite duration, we reserve the right to seek clarification or to challenge it before a competent Somali court, so that a user's right to be informed is not suspended indefinitely.\n\n## 10. Authentication and Fraud Prevention\n\nWe take steps to **verify the authenticity** of requests and the authority of the requester. We may decline to act on, or seek further verification of, any request that we cannot authenticate or that appears irregular, fraudulent, or improper. Fraudulent requests for customer data are taken seriously and may themselves be reported to the Authorities.\n\n## 11. Data Protection and Minimisation\n\nWe disclose personal data only to the extent permitted or required by applicable law and valid legal process, and we seek to limit disclosure to the information that is actually requested and necessary. Our handling of personal data is described in our **Privacy Policy**, and our financial-crime controls are summarised in our **AML/KYC Policy**.\n\n## 12. Cost Reimbursement\n\nWhere permitted by law, we may seek reimbursement of the reasonable costs we incur in responding to a request, particularly for voluminous, complex, or repeated requests.\n\n## 13. Reservation of Rights\n\nNothing in these Guidelines waives any right, objection, privilege, or defence available to OMAYA or our users, or constitutes consent to jurisdiction. We reserve the right to **object to, challenge, narrow, or decline** any request, and to require that requests follow the proper legal channels.\n\n## 14. Foreign and Cross-Border Requests\n\nAuthorities outside Somalia should generally proceed through recognised legal channels — such as a **mutual legal assistance treaty (MLAT), letters rogatory, or other channels recognised under Somali law** — unless another lawful basis for the request exists. We may decline to act on a direct request from a foreign Authority that is not supported by an appropriate legal basis.\n\n## 15. No Legal Advice and No Third-Party Rights\n\nThese Guidelines are provided for information only. They are not legal advice, do not create any contractual or other rights or obligations, and do not limit the legal requirements that apply to OMAYA or to any Authority.\n\n## 16. Changes to These Guidelines\n\nWe may update these Guidelines from time to time. We will post the updated version and update the \"Last Updated\" date.\n\n## 17. Contact\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Law enforcement and government requests: **lawenforcement@omaya.io**\n- Compliance enquiries: **compliance@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*These Guidelines should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel familiar with Somali law and with the requirements for responding to domestic and foreign legal process, and the response thresholds, preservation periods, and contact routes should be confirmed against OMAYA's internal procedures before publication.*\n","OMAYA-Payment-Policy-v1.1.md":"# Payment Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis Payment Policy explains the fees, exchange rates, deposits, withdrawals, refunds, cancellations, and chargebacks that apply when you use the services of **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\"). It forms part of our **Terms of Service** and should be read together with them and with our **Risk Disclosure Statement**. It applies to all of our services, including our digital asset Exchange, crypto-to-crypto Swap, MoneyX local payment transfers, peer-to-peer (P2P) trading, foreign exchange, and remittance and payment services (the \"**Services**\").\n\n> **Important:** You are responsible for checking that every payment detail is correct **before** you confirm a transaction. Many transactions — in particular Digital Asset transfers — are **final and cannot be reversed, recovered, or refunded** if you make a mistake. See Sections 8 and 10.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nThis Policy covers the fees and charges that apply to the Services, how exchange rates are applied, how deposits and withdrawals are processed, and how refunds, cancellations, chargebacks, and similar matters are handled. The specific fees, spreads, limits, and supported payment methods that apply to you are shown on the Platform at the time of your transaction and may be set out in a separate fee schedule (for example, at omaya.io/fees).\n\n## 2. Fees, Spreads, and Commissions\n\nYou agree to pay all applicable fees, spreads, commissions, and charges for the Services. Depending on the Service, these may include exchange or trading fees, Swap fees, MoneyX and transfer fees, remittance fees, deposit and withdrawal fees, currency-conversion margins, card-processing fees, and administrative fees. Fees may be charged as a fixed amount, a percentage, a spread or margin built into the rate we quote, or a combination of these, and are displayed or otherwise made available to you before or at the time you confirm a transaction.\n\nWe may **change our fees at any time**. Changes take effect when published, and your continued use of the Services after a change constitutes acceptance of the revised fees. Except as required by law or as expressly stated in this Policy, **fees, spreads, and commissions are non-refundable**, including where a transaction is later reversed or refunded for reasons attributable to you.\n\n## 3. Exchange Rates and Quotes\n\nExchange rates and quotes are set by reference to market conditions and include our spread or margin. Rates and quotes are **indicative until a transaction is confirmed**, and the applicable rate is the rate confirmed at the time of the transaction. A quote may **expire** if the transaction is not completed within the required time, if market rates move, or if the transaction is subject to compliance review, in which case we may re-quote, cancel, or decline it.\n\n## 4. Network (Blockchain) Fees\n\nDigital Asset transactions are subject to **blockchain network fees** (sometimes called \"gas\" or \"miner\" fees), which are determined by the relevant network and not by OMAYA. Network fees can change rapidly and may be **deducted from the amount you send or receive**, or charged in addition to our fees. You are responsible for network fees, and they are generally **non-refundable**, including on any return or refund of Digital Assets (see Section 10).\n\n## 5. Payment Methods, Ownership, and Limits\n\nWe make various payment methods available, which may include local banks, mobile money services, e-wallets, Digital Assets, and — where offered — debit or credit cards. The available methods are shown on the Platform and may be added, restricted, or removed at any time. Many payment methods involve third-party providers, whose processing times and rules are outside our control.\n\nUnless we approve otherwise, any payment account you use (such as a bank or mobile money account) must be **registered in your own name and match your verified identity**. Payments from or to **third-party accounts, mismatched names, business or agent accounts, or unverified sources** may be **delayed, rejected, returned, frozen, or subject to enhanced due diligence**.\n\n**Limits.** Minimum and maximum transaction limits may vary by Service, payment method, asset, network, Account type, KYC level, risk rating, jurisdiction, and operational availability, and are shown on the Platform.\n\n## 6. Deposits\n\nDeposits are credited to your Account after we have received and, where applicable, confirmed the funds — for Digital Assets, after the required number of network confirmations. A payment is treated as **final only when OMAYA determines that it has been received, reconciled, cleared, and is not subject to reversal, recall, chargeback, provider rejection, or fraud review**; a receipt, screenshot, or notification does not by itself prove final receipt. Some payment methods are processed only during business hours or before applicable **cut-off times**, and transactions submitted afterward may be processed on the next business day or when the relevant third-party provider is available. We may place a **hold on, delay, or decline** a deposit for compliance, security, fraud-prevention, or legal reasons.\n\n## 7. Withdrawals\n\nWithdrawals are subject to verification, limits, fees, and applicable network fees, and may be **delayed, held, or declined** for compliance, security, fraud-prevention, or legal reasons. For Digital Asset withdrawals, you must provide the **correct destination address and select the correct network**. Processing times are not guaranteed and may be affected by verification, network conditions, cut-off times, and third-party providers.\n\n## 8. Your Responsibility for Transaction Details\n\n**You are solely responsible for the accuracy of all transaction details that you provide**, including wallet addresses, blockchain networks, bank and mobile money account numbers, account names, payment references, beneficiary details, and amounts.\n\n- **Digital Assets.** Blockchain transfers are **final and generally irreversible**. If you send Digital Assets to a **wrong or incompatible address**, select the **wrong network**, or send an **unsupported asset or token**, the assets may be **permanently lost**. OMAYA may be **unable to recover them, and cannot refund assets that it is unable to recover.** It is your responsibility to verify the asset, network, and address are correct before you send.\n- **Fiat and local payments.** If you provide incorrect or mismatched payment details, your payment may fail, be delayed, be sent to the wrong recipient, or be impossible to reverse.\n\nOMAYA is not responsible for any loss arising from incorrect, incomplete, outdated, or mismatched details that you provide.\n\n## 9. Underpayment, Overpayment, Late, and Split Payments\n\nIf you **underpay, overpay, pay after a quote has expired, split a single payment into multiple payments, or omit a required payment reference**, we may delay, cancel, re-quote, partially process, or refund the net amount (after applicable fees), or request additional information, in each case acting reasonably and subject to compliance review.\n\n## 10. Refunds\n\n10.1. **General.** Completed transactions are generally **not refundable**. Refunds are made only where required by law, where we expressly agree, or as set out in this Section.\n\n10.2. **Mistakes you make.** Where a transaction cannot be completed, or funds cannot be recovered, because of incorrect details you provided, we are **not obliged to refund** you, and any refund is subject to the deductions below and to our ability to recover the funds.\n\n10.3. **Digital Assets sent in error.** If you send Digital Assets to a wrong address or network, or send an unsupported asset, the transfer is generally **irreversible and may be permanently lost**. OMAYA has **no obligation to attempt recovery and cannot refund what it cannot recover.** Where OMAYA does agree to attempt a recovery or return, recovery is not guaranteed, and OMAYA will deduct the relevant **network fees and any costs incurred** and may charge an **administrative fee**; any applicable recovery or administrative fee will be **shown in the fee schedule or communicated to you before recovery is attempted**.\n\n10.4. **Refunds or returns of Digital Assets.** Where any refund or return of Digital Assets is made, we will deduct the applicable **network fees and any costs we incur**, and return only the net amount.\n\n10.5. **Refunds or returns of fiat where you made the mistake.** Where we return fiat funds that you sent in error, or that could not be processed because of incorrect details you provided, we will deduct **all applicable commissions, fees, charges, and any exchange-rate difference or cost we incur**, and return only the **net amount**. Where a currency conversion is involved, the return is made at the **prevailing exchange rate**, which may be less favourable than the original rate.\n\n10.6. **How and when refunds are made.** Where a refund is due, we will normally return funds to the **original source** where possible, after any verification we require. Refunds, where approved, may take **several business days or longer**, depending on the payment method, network, third-party provider, and any compliance review, and on whether the refund involves Digital Assets, cards, banks, or mobile money.\n\n## 11. Cancellations\n\nOnce you confirm a transaction, it is your authorisation for us to proceed, and Digital Asset and many other transactions **cannot be cancelled** once submitted. We may **cancel, void, re-price, or decline** a transaction where required for compliance, security, or legal reasons, where a quote has expired, or where it was affected by a manifest or system error (see Section 9.5 of our Terms of Service).\n\n## 12. Failed, Delayed, Duplicate, or Reversed Payments\n\nIf a payment **fails, is delayed, is duplicated, is recalled, is reversed, or is charged back**, we may delay completion, request additional evidence, return funds where possible, **deduct any duplicate or incorrect credit**, or restrict your Account, in each case to correct the issue and manage risk. We are not responsible for delays or failures caused by third-party banks, mobile money operators, payment processors, or networks.\n\n## 13. Compliance Holds and Blocked or Frozen Funds\n\nDeposits, withdrawals, transfers, and other payments may be **delayed, rejected, frozen, returned, restricted, reversed, or cancelled** as a result of KYC, AML/CFT, sanctions, Travel Rule, wallet-ownership, source-of-funds, counterparty, or fraud-prevention checks, or where required by law, a court order, or a regulator or law-enforcement request, or under our internal risk controls. **We may be legally prohibited from explaining the reason for, or confirming the existence of, such action.** Further detail is in our **AML/KYC Policy** and **Law Enforcement Request Guidelines**.\n\n## 14. Card Payments (Where Offered)\n\nWhere we accept debit or credit card payments, those payments may be processed by **third-party card processors** and are subject to the rules of the relevant **card networks**. OMAYA and/or its payment processors handle cardholder data in accordance with applicable card-network rules and payment-security standards, **including the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) where applicable**, and we do not store full card details unless expressly stated. OMAYA may **refuse, delay, reverse, or require additional verification** for any card payment suspected of fraud, unauthorised use, or chargeback risk. Any card refund is normally made to the **original card**.\n\n## 15. Chargebacks and Reversals\n\nInitiating a chargeback, recall, or payment dispute **without a valid, lawful basis is a breach** of our Terms of Service. Where this happens, we may suspend or close your Account, **freeze or reverse affected balances, recover amounts owed, apply an administrative charge, report the conduct, and pursue legal remedies**. Where you raise or are involved in a chargeback or payment dispute, we may require **evidence** — such as a payment receipt, bank or mobile money statement, cardholder confirmation, transaction reference, proof that you own the payment account, identity verification, and an explanation of the dispute.\n\n## 16. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Payments\n\nIn P2P trades, payment is made **directly between users**, and OMAYA acts only as a facilitator and, where applicable, an escrow or asset-locking provider.\n\n- A **buyer** must pay the **exact amount**, within the required time, using **only the payment method shown** in the confirmed order and a payment account **registered in the buyer's own name**.\n- A **seller** must confirm that the correct payment has **actually been received** in their own account before releasing Digital Assets; a **screenshot, receipt, or notification is not proof of final receipt**.\n- Submitting a **false or altered receipt**, or falsely marking an order as paid, is a serious breach and may lead to cancellation, account restriction, reporting, and legal action.\n- If a payment is **reversed, recalled, or charged back after Digital Assets have been released**, the amount becomes a **debt owed to OMAYA or the seller**, and we may set it off, freeze balances, or take other lawful action.\n- We may **hold or freeze the Digital Assets and funds involved in a P2P trade during a dispute** while we review the available evidence.\n\n## 17. Set-Off and Negative Balances\n\nWe may **set off and deduct** from any balance in your Account (fiat or Digital Asset) any amount you owe us, including unpaid fees, negative balances, reversed or charged-back payments, duplicate credits, and amounts arising from your breach of our Terms. Where a balance is insufficient, you must **repay the shortfall on demand**, and we may convert Digital Assets to fiat (or the reverse) at prevailing rates to give effect to this Section.\n\n## 18. Dormant-Account and Other Fees\n\nWhere permitted by law, we may charge a **dormant-account maintenance fee** on an Account that has had no login or transaction activity for an extended period, as described in our Terms of Service. We may also charge **administrative fees** for specific services, such as attempted recovery of misdirected or unsupported assets, as described in this Policy or on the Platform.\n\n## 19. Payment Rules by Service\n\nIn addition to the general rules above, the following apply to specific Services:\n\n- **Exchange (crypto ↔ local payment).** When you buy Digital Assets, they are credited after your local payment is received and cleared; when you sell Digital Assets, your local payment is sent after your Digital Assets are received and confirmed, at the rate confirmed at the time.\n- **Swap (crypto ↔ crypto).** Swaps are priced at the rate confirmed at the time, may be routed through third-party liquidity providers, and are final once confirmed; network fees apply to each asset and network.\n- **MoneyX (local payment transfers).** Transfers depend on the sending and receiving providers; the receiving account must match the beneficiary details you provide, and provider delays, outages, and reversal decisions are outside our control.\n- **Remittance.** Payouts may be made by bank transfer, mobile money, or cash pickup where available, may involve agents, and may require the recipient to complete verification before payout; cancellation and refund depend on whether the funds have already been paid out, and any refund may be made at the prevailing exchange rate.\n- **Forex (local agent).** OMAYA acts **only as a local agent and payment conduit** for third-party Brokers. The **Broker sets all spreads, commissions, and financing charges**, which are governed by the Broker's own terms. For deposits, our responsibility ends once funds reach the Broker; for withdrawals, it begins only on our receipt of funds from the Broker. See Section 7 of our Terms of Service.\n- **P2P.** See Section 16.\n\n## 20. Taxes\n\nOur fees are exclusive of any taxes unless stated otherwise. **You are solely responsible** for determining, reporting, and paying any taxes that apply to your use of the Services and your transactions, as described in our Terms of Service.\n\n## 21. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Payment Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version on the Platform and update the \"Last Updated\" date. Where the changes are material, we will take reasonable steps to notify you.\n\n## 22. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Payments, fees, and refund enquiries: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This Payment Policy should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication, and the fees, spreads, limits, cut-off times, refund handling, and dormant-account terms referred to here should be confirmed against OMAYA's actual pricing and operational practices and kept consistent with the fee information shown on the Platform.*\n","OMAYA-Referral-Program-Terms-v1.1.md":"# Referral Program Terms\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThese Referral Program Terms (\"**Referral Terms**\") govern the OMAYA referral program (the \"**Program**\") operated by **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\"). The Program lets eligible users invite others to OMAYA and earn rewards when certain conditions are met. By participating in the Program — as a person who refers another (a \"**Referrer**\") or as a person who is referred (a \"**Referred User**\") — you agree to these Referral Terms. They form part of, and should be read together with, our **Terms of Service** and **Privacy Policy**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. About the Referral Program\n\nThe Program is a **promotional offer** provided at our discretion. It is **not a right or entitlement**, does not form part of our core Services, and may be changed, suspended, or withdrawn as set out in these Referral Terms. The current details of the Program — including how to refer others, the rewards available, and the conditions for earning them — are shown on the Platform.\n\n## 2. Eligibility\n\nTo participate, you must:\n\n- have a registered OMAYA Account that is **fully verified** (KYC completed) and **in good standing**;\n- be **at least 18 years old** and legally able to participate;\n- not be located in, or a resident of, a country or region where the Program or our Services are restricted; and\n- not be subject to any suspension, restriction, sanctions designation, or prohibition under our Terms of Service.\n\nOMAYA **employees, officers, contractors, agents, affiliates, ambassadors, and their immediate family members are not eligible** to participate unless OMAYA expressly permits it in writing.\n\nThe Program is **void where prohibited by law**. We may restrict, modify, or withhold rewards in any jurisdiction where the Program would require a registration, approval, licence, tax withholding, or other compliance step that OMAYA has not completed.\n\n## 3. How the Program Works\n\nEligible Referrers receive a **unique referral link or code** that they may share with people they **personally know** (see Section 10). A Referred User must use that link or code when registering. A referral may qualify for a reward once the Referred User has completed registration and identity verification and the **qualifying conditions in Section 5 are met**. We track referrals using the referral link or code and other information, and **our records are determinative** of whether a referral qualifies.\n\n**Genuinely new users only.** A person is **not** a genuinely new user if they already have, or previously had, an Account (including a closed account), or if they use the **same identity, phone number, email, device, payment method, wallet, or other indicators of control** as an existing user, or are otherwise determined by OMAYA to be a duplicate or related user.\n\n**Tracking and attribution.** We are **not responsible** for referrals that are not tracked because of incorrect or expired links or codes, browser or cookie settings, cookie blocking, app-store or device restrictions, technical issues, or the Referred User failing to use the referral link or code at registration.\n\n## 4. Referral Rewards\n\nThe rewards available under the Program — including their **type, amount, form, currency or asset, and any caps or limits** — are shown on the Platform and may be **changed at any time**. Rewards may take the form of, for example, Digital Assets, fee discounts, or account credits, as we determine. Where a reward is paid in **Digital Assets, its value may fluctuate**, and OMAYA does not guarantee any fiat value. We may also **convert or substitute** the type of reward. Rewards have **no guaranteed cash value**, are not transferable except as we allow, and are subject to these Referral Terms.\n\n## 5. Qualifying Conditions\n\nTo earn a reward, all conditions shown on the Platform must be met. These may include that the Referred User:\n\n- completes **identity verification (KYC)**;\n- is a genuinely new, independent user (see Section 3); and\n- completes a **minimum qualifying activity** (such as a minimum deposit, trade, exchange, or transaction volume) within any applicable time period.\n\nWe may apply **holding periods, minimum thresholds, time windows, and limits on the number of qualifying referrals**, and a reward is only earned once we confirm that the conditions have been satisfied. We may also apply **reward caps and limits** by user, Account, household, device, IP address, payment method, campaign, jurisdiction, or time period.\n\n## 6. When Rewards Are Paid and When They Are Forfeited\n\nWhere a referral qualifies, the reward is credited to the relevant Account in the manner and within the timeframe shown on the Platform, and may require the Account to remain **active and in good standing**. Rewards may **expire if not claimed or used** within the period shown on the Platform.\n\nA reward may be **withheld, delayed, reduced, cancelled, reversed, clawed back, or forfeited**, and may be treated as a **debt owed to OMAYA**, where the qualifying conditions are not met, where the Account is restricted or closed, where these Referral Terms or our Terms of Service are breached, or where a reward remains unclaimed beyond any stated expiry. In particular, if a **qualifying deposit, trade, exchange, payment, or transaction is later refunded, reversed, charged back, cancelled, suspected of abuse, or found not to qualify**, any related reward may be withheld, reversed, clawed back, or treated as a debt.\n\n## 7. Prohibited and Abusive Conduct\n\nThe Program is for **genuine referrals** only. The following are **prohibited**, and any referral or reward connected with them may be disqualified:\n\n- **referring yourself**, or rewarding your own activity;\n- creating or using **multiple, fake, duplicate, or fraudulent accounts**, **mule accounts**, or **account farming**;\n- referrals between accounts controlled by the **same person**, or **coordinated, collusive, or \"referral farm\" arrangements** in which a person or group completes registration or KYC mainly to generate or share rewards;\n- **wash trading, circular trading, circular MoneyX or payment flows, collusive P2P trades, deposits funded by the Referrer**, or other artificial activity carried out mainly to meet qualifying conditions;\n- **paid sign-ups**, or the use of **shared devices, shared payment accounts, or high-risk third-party payments** to manufacture referrals;\n- **false, stolen, or manipulated identity or verification** information;\n- using **bots, scripts, or other automated means**, or exploiting any error, bug, or loophole in the Program;\n- **spam, misleading, or unauthorised promotion** (see Section 10); and\n- any conduct that breaches our Terms of Service or our AML, sanctions, or fraud-prevention requirements.\n\nWe may use **behavioural analysis, device fingerprinting, and other detection techniques** to identify duplicate, collusive, or fraudulent referral activity and networks.\n\n## 8. Investigation, Claw-Back, and Adjustment\n\nWe may **monitor and investigate** participation in the Program. Where we reasonably suspect ineligibility, abuse, fraud, or breach of these Referral Terms, we may, to the extent permitted by law, **withhold, reduce, cancel, reverse, recover, claw back, or set off** any reward (whether or not already credited), **suspend or close** the Accounts involved, and take any other action available under our Terms of Service. Where a reward has already been paid, the amount may be treated as a **debt owed to us** and recovered, including by deduction from your Account balances. Our determinations under this Section are final.\n\n## 9. Identity Verification and Compliance\n\nAll participation and rewards are subject to our **KYC, AML/CFT, sanctions, and fraud-prevention** requirements. We may **withhold or delay a reward** pending verification, and we may refuse or reverse a reward where verification is not completed or where paying it would be unlawful or inconsistent with those requirements.\n\n## 10. How You May Promote OMAYA\n\nReferral links and codes are intended to be shared **privately, with people you personally know**. Public or large-scale promotion (including affiliate-style or paid influencer promotion) is **not permitted** under these Referral Terms unless we expressly agree in writing under separate terms.\n\nWhen sharing your referral link or code, you must comply with the following.\n\n**10.1 Disclose the reward relationship.** You must **clearly and conspicuously disclose** that you may receive a reward if the person you refer signs up or completes qualifying activity. Any disclosure must be honest and placed close to the referral message. Anyone with a significant audience who promotes OMAYA must include a clear disclosure such as **\"#ad\" or \"Paid Promotion.\"**\n\n**10.2 No profit or investment claims.** You must **not** describe OMAYA, Digital Assets, forex, P2P, or any Service as **guaranteed, risk-free, profitable, an investment, investment advice, or a way to earn particular returns**, and you must not use misleading terms such as \"guaranteed profit,\" \"safe investment,\" \"double your money,\" or \"risk-free crypto.\"\n\n**10.3 No spam.** You must **not** send referral messages to people who have not agreed to receive them, post your link where it is not permitted, upload or scrape contact lists without permission, or use automated messaging tools, bots, or bulk-messaging services.\n\n**10.4 Brand, social media, and advertising.** You must **not** impersonate OMAYA or suggest you speak for or are endorsed by OMAYA; create **fake OMAYA pages** or unofficial groups implying endorsement; use OMAYA's **name, logos, or brand** (other than approved assets) in paid advertising, domain names, or search keywords; run **paid advertising targeting restricted countries**; or use **misleading screenshots or fake testimonials**.\n\n**10.5 Your responsibility for the law.** You are responsible for ensuring your referral activity complies with all laws that apply where you promote the Program, including **advertising, consumer-protection, financial-promotion, anti-spam, data-protection, and social-media platform** rules.\n\n## 11. No Agency or Employment\n\nParticipating in the Program does **not** make you an employee, agent, partner, or representative of OMAYA. You have **no authority** to make commitments on our behalf, and you act only for yourself.\n\n## 12. Taxes\n\nYou are **solely responsible** for determining, reporting, and paying any taxes that apply to any reward you receive under the Program, as described in our Terms of Service. Where applicable law triggers **tax-reporting, information-reporting, or withholding** obligations, we may require you to provide **tax-identification information (such as a taxpayer identification number)** before issuing further rewards, and we may **withhold, deduct, or report** rewards as required by law.\n\n## 13. Referral Program Privacy\n\nTo operate, monitor, and prevent abuse of the Program, we process information such as **referral codes and links, attribution data, Account identifiers, device and fraud-prevention data, and qualifying-activity information**, as described in our **Privacy Policy**.\n\nWe may show a Referrer **limited referral-status information** — such as whether a referral is pending, qualified, rejected, or rewarded — but we will **not disclose detailed identity (KYC), transaction, or other personal information** about a Referred User to the Referrer, except where permitted by law or with consent.\n\n## 14. Changes, Suspension, and Termination of the Program\n\nWe may **change, suspend, or terminate** the Program, or any part of it, and may change these Referral Terms or the available rewards and conditions, **at any time and at our discretion**. We may also **end your participation** in the Program. We will post material changes on the Platform. Rewards already validly earned before a change or termination will be handled in accordance with the Referral Terms in effect when they were earned, except where we are required to act otherwise by law or for compliance reasons.\n\n## 15. Our Discretion and Final Decisions\n\nWe administer the Program at our discretion, including decisions about eligibility, whether qualifying conditions are met, and whether conduct is abusive. **Our decisions on these matters are final**, subject to any rights you have under applicable law.\n\n## 16. No Warranty and Limitation of Liability\n\nThe Program and any rewards are provided **\"as is\"** and **\"as available,\"** with no warranty that the Program will continue or be uninterrupted or error-free. To the maximum extent permitted by law, our liability in connection with the Program is subject to the **limitations and exclusions of liability set out in our Terms of Service**.\n\n## 17. Relationship to Our Other Terms\n\nThese Referral Terms **supplement** our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy. If there is a conflict between these Referral Terms and our Terms of Service **specifically in relation to the Program**, these Referral Terms govern; in all other respects, our **Terms of Service prevail**. Terms used but not defined here have the meaning given in our Terms of Service.\n\n## 18. General\n\nThese Referral Terms are governed by the laws of the **Federal Republic of Somalia**, consistent with the governing-law and dispute-resolution provisions of our Terms of Service. If any provision is found to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in effect. Our failure to enforce any provision is not a waiver of it. These Referral Terms may be made available in **English and other languages**; if there is any inconsistency, the **English version prevails** to the extent permitted by law.\n\n## 19. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Referral program enquiries: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*These Referral Program Terms should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication, and the rewards, qualifying conditions, limits, expiry periods, and any tax-reporting thresholds referred to here should be confirmed against the Program details shown on the Platform and any applicable promotion, consumer-protection, and tax requirements.*\n"};
